 "researcher_notes": "No existing GEM row for Momentum under the Transcontinental Gas Pipeline name (21 Transco rows checked; none is Momentum). FERC docket CP01-388. EIA August 2026 release, sheet Historical Projects (1996-2024): Phase I is Excel row 285 and Phase II is Excel row 321. Phase I: 42.26 miles of new pipe, 42 and 48 inch, 262 MMcf/d added, 163.85 million USD, Louisiana to North Carolina, in service May 2003. Phase II: 25.86 miles, 42 inch, 53 MMcf/d added, 24.82 million USD, Alabama to Virginia, in service February 2004. Both are over the 25 km (15.5 mile) length rule (68 km and 42 km), so the phases are split into two rows. Costs sum to 188.67 million USD, close to the 197 million USD in the Federal Register notice of 4 October 2001 (FERC amendment to downsize the project). That notice and the July 2001 notice describe the proposal, not the as-built lengths, so they support owner and proposal year only. As-built lengths, capacity, cost and in-service dates rest on the single EIA release, so tier is medium. Not checked: a FERC order or operator release for as-built figures, and the exact start and end points. The 2001 notice lists loops on the Transco mainline between Mississippi and South Carolina. Route not researched: set RouteType and RouteAccuracy later from loop mile posts; the Phase I/II split of the loops is not stated in the sources read. Start and end towns left blank. Status is operating: EIA lists both phases as completed."
}